# Desktop packaging (issue #84): the installer stages the ettin reranker
# (web_ui manifest group `core`) and the gemma LLM (group `llm`) weights under
# <resourcesPath>/models — loaded by the native backend — and EXCLUDES those
# dirs from the packaged renderer copy. This mode bakes the excluded groups
# into the bundle so the readiness gate (checkPackagedModels ->
# EXCLUDED_MODEL_GROUPS) does not report them as "required model file(s) not
# found" (review PRR-132). Group granularity is coarse by design: marking
# `core` also skips the readiness presence check for the ort entry, and `llm`
# for the wllama entry — both DO ship in the renderer copy, and NOTHING
# presence-checks them at packaged runtime afterwards (a missing file would
# surface as a first-inference fetch failure, not a boot error; the build-time
# safety net is the stager's assertRendererManifestComplete). Kept in lockstep
# with desktop/scripts/stage-installer-resources.mjs by the cross-manifest
# parity spec (desktop/src/__tests__/e1-manifest-contract.test.ts).
VITE_EXCLUDE_MODEL_GROUPS=core,llm
